findings.body:
Removing `@require_role("admin")` strips the only access control on `DELETE /users/<user>`. Any client can now delete any user and get `204`, which is a direct privilege escalation / broken-authorization failure for a destructive endpoint.

The comment says cleanup jobs as the viewer account were blocked — that means the job identity lacks permission, not that the guard should disappear. Give the cleanup job an admin (or dedicated service) role and keep `@require_role` on this route so viewer-scoped callers still cannot delete users.

```suggestion
@require_role("admin")
def delete_user(user):
```
